			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Rename dotfile root from .land to .fiddee\n\nExtract the FIDDEE user-data directory path ($HOME/.fiddee) into a shared FiddeeRoot() atom at Source/Platform/FiddeeRoot.ts, replacing the scattered `process.env.HOME/.land/...` string literals across three storage-path resolution sites and one extension-bug stack filter.\n\nThe new file mirrors the Rust atom at Element/Mountain/Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Utilities/FiddeeRoot.rs, centralising the product-name mapping so a future rename touches one file per language. The fallback semantics match the previous `$HOME/.land` resolution.\n\nUpdate Source/Services/Extension/Context.ts to derive GlobalStorageRoot from FiddeeRoot() instead of hardcoding the $HOME/.land prefix. Rewrite Source/Services/Handler/Extension/Host/Handler.ts to use FiddeeRoot() for extensionStorage, globalStorage, and logs, preserving the dedicated (non-scanned) root discipline that keeps storage out of the Mountain extension scanner path. Add `/.fiddee/extensions/` to the extension-internal-bug frame matcher in Source/Services/Handler/Notification/Handler.ts so the rejection filter works for both old and new dotfile layouts.\n\nBuild artifacts in Target/ are rebuilt to reflect the new FiddeeRoot path dependency across the ESBuild output graph.",
			"SHA": "16ab1dd18507535605e3386477f56c20bb638950"
		}
